# Small Object Detection Using YOLO

CSCI 611 – Assignment 3  
Olivia Johnson

## Project Overview

This project implements small object detection using the YOLOv8 object detection framework. The goal is to detect traffic signs from road images and video sequences. Because traffic signs are often small and distant, additional training and parameter tuning were performed to improve detection performance.

The project evaluates:

1. A pretrained YOLOv8 model
2. A fine-tuned YOLOv8 model trained at image resolution 640
3. A fine-tuned YOLOv8 model trained at image resolution 1280

The results show that increasing image resolution significantly improves detection performance for small traffic signs.

---

## Dataset

The dataset used in this project is the **Mapillary Traffic Sign Dataset (MTSD)**.

Original dataset link:  
https://www.mapillary.com/dataset/trafficsign

A subset of the dataset was used and converted into YOLO format.

Dataset split:

- Training images: 9933
- Validation images: 1241
- Test images: 1243

Annotations were converted from JSON format to YOLO format:

```
<class_id> <x_center> <y_center> <width> <height>
```

