## Environment Setup

Install dependencies:

```bash
pip install ultralytics opencv-python numpy torch torchvision torchaudio
```

---
## You will also need to install the data sets yourself as they are too large to include here. You can use the convert_to_yolo file to convert the json to the correct format for YOLO.

## Running YOLO Detection

Example usage:

```python
from ultralytics import YOLO

model = YOLO("yolov8n.pt")
results = model("sample_image.jpg")
results.show()
```

---

## Training the Model

Example training command:

```python
from ultralytics import YOLO

model = YOLO("yolov8n.pt")

model.train(
    data="dataset.yaml",
    epochs=30,
    imgsz=640,
    batch=16
)
```

Another experiment was performed using higher resolution to improve detection of small objects:

```python
model.train(
    data="dataset.yaml",
    epochs=30,
    imgsz=1280,
    batch=8
)
```

---

## Detection on Video

Example:

```python
model("traffic.mov", conf=0.5, save=True)
```

Frames were extracted from the resulting detection video for analysis.

---

## Results

Performance comparison:

| Model | mAP50 | mAP50-95 | Precision | Recall |
|------|------|------|------|------|
| Pretrained YOLOv8n | 0.010 | 0.006 | 0.017 | 0.071 |
| YOLOv8n (640) | 0.272 | 0.188 | 0.428 | 0.289 |
| YOLOv8n (1280) | 0.510 | 0.383 | 0.596 | 0.487 |

Increasing image resolution significantly improved detection of small traffic signs.

---

## Files Included

This repository contains:

